# HoloDex (VerLab)

Omnidirectional lab robot: 4× NEMA23 steppers + mecanum wheels. Private VerLab repo.

## Control architecture (firmware-centric)

Kinematics, odometry, and teleop live on the ESP32. The PC Python UI is legacy/optional.

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `firmware/` | ESP32 PlatformIO firmware — IK, odometry, SoftAP web teleop, Zenoh ROS bridge |
| `src/` | Legacy PySide6 client (raw motor Hz over Zenoh); prefer web UI |
| `docker/` | Eclipse Zenoh router (`7447`, `8000`) |

### Runtime flow

```
Web joystick (SoftAP) ─┐
                       ├─► MotionController (watchdog, web > zenoh)
Zenoh holodex/cmd_vel ─┘         │
                                 ▼
                      HolonomicKinematics (IK)
                                 │
                      FastAccelStepper ×4
                                 │
                      Odometry (FK + optional gyro Z)
                                 ├─► WebSocket odom stream
                                 └─► Zenoh holodex/odom
```

- SoftAP SSID default `HoloDex` / `holodex123` → `http://192.168.4.1/` (WS `:81`)
- WIFI_AP_STA: AP always on; STA optional for Zenoh/lab network (NVS config via web)
- Zenoh topics (ROS-oriented JSON): `holodex/cmd_vel` (sub), `holodex/odom` (pub)
- Geometry (mecanum): `r=0.05 m`, `lx=0.19 m`, `ly=0.195 m`, `L=lx+ly`, `steps_per_rev=6400` (32 µstep); IK `v=vx±vy±L·ω` about chassis center; driver 2 A via Vref

## Contribution

- Branch from `dev`; PRs → `dev` → `main`. Conventional Commits.
- Details: `CONTRIBUTING.md`.

## When editing

- Keep body-frame `Twist2D` (vx, vy, omega) as the control interface — do not move IK back to the host.
- Align web + Zenoh command paths through `MotionController`.
- Do not commit WiFi secrets; use SoftAP config page / NVS.
- All user-facing firmware strings and new docs: English.
